    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Adverbs of frequency answer the question <strong>How often?</strong> From 100 % to 0 %: <em>always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely / hardly ever, never</em>. <em>I <strong>always</strong> have tea. She <strong>rarely</strong> cooks. They <strong>never</strong> eat meat.</em>",
        "tag": "How often?"
      },
      {
        "html": "With most verbs, the adverb goes <strong>before the main verb</strong>: <em>I <strong>always</strong> walk to school. She <strong>usually</strong> reads on the bus. We <strong>often</strong> eat out.</em>",
        "tag": "Before the main verb"
      },
      {
        "html": "With the verb <strong>be</strong>, the adverb goes <strong>after be</strong>: <em>He is <strong>always</strong> happy. They are <strong>never</strong> late. I'm <strong>usually</strong> at home on Sundays.</em>",
        "tag": "After be"
      },
      {
        "html": "With <strong>can</strong>, the adverb goes after <em>can</em>: <em>I can <strong>never</strong> find my keys.</em> With <strong>don't</strong>, use <em>often</em>, <em>usually</em> or <em>always</em> after <em>don't</em>: <em>I don't <strong>often</strong> go out.</em> <em>Never</em>, <em>rarely</em> and <em>hardly ever</em> are already negative, so do not add <em>don't</em>: <em>I <strong>never</strong> go out.</em>",
        "tag": "can and don't"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>Sometimes</strong> can go in three places: <em>I sometimes take the bus. Sometimes I take the bus. I take the bus sometimes.</em> <em>Usually</em> and <em>often</em> can also start a sentence: <em>Usually I walk.</em> <em>Always</em> and <em>never</em> stay in the middle.",
        "tag": "Sometimes can move"
      },
      {
        "html": "Ask with <strong>How often …?</strong> Answer with a time expression at the <strong>end</strong>: <em>How often do you go swimming? – I go swimming <strong>twice a week</strong>.</em> More examples: <em>every day, once a month, three times a year</em>.",
        "tag": "How often? / every day"
      },
      {
        "html": "✗ <em>I go always to school.</em> → ✓ <em>I always go to school.</em> · ✗ <em>She always is happy.</em> → ✓ <em>She is always happy.</em> · ✗ <em>I don't never eat meat.</em> → ✓ <em>I never eat meat.</em> · ✗ <em>I twice a week go swimming.</em> → ✓ <em>I go swimming twice a week.</em>",
        "tag": "Typical mistakes"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Adverbs of frequency are very common with the <a href=\"/present-simple\">present simple</a>: <em>I always have a shower in the morning.</em> For questions with <em>How often</em> and other question words, see <a href=\"/wh-questions\">Question words</a>.",
